1
00:00:02,550 --> 00:00:03,551
KATARA: Water.

2
00:00:04,928 --> 00:00:05,929
Earth.

3
00:00:06,846 --> 00:00:07,847
Fire.

4
00:00:08,890 --> 00:00:09,891
Air.

5
00:00:11,434 --> 00:00:15,396
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,522 --> 00:00:18,566
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,859 --> 00:00:22,487
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

8
00:00:22,612 --> 00:00:23,821
could stop them.

9
00:00:23,947 --> 00:00:26,241
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

10
00:00:27,575 --> 00:00:29,702
A hundred years passed,
and my brother and I discovered

11
00:00:29,827 --> 00:00:32,914
the new Avatar,
an Airbender named Aang.

12
00:00:33,039 --> 00:00:35,250
And although
his airbending skills are great,

13
00:00:35,375 --> 00:00:37,669
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

14
00:00:37,794 --> 00:00:39,003
AANG: Oof!

15
00:00:39,128 --> 00:00:42,090
KATARA: But I believe
Aang can save the world.

16
00:00:42,215 --> 00:00:45,718
♪

17
00:00:56,169 --> 00:01:00,257
♪

18
00:01:02,384 --> 00:01:04,052
♪

19
00:01:05,178 --> 00:01:09,558
[ missiles exploding ]

20
00:01:10,308 --> 00:01:16,273
♪

21
00:01:17,232 --> 00:01:18,608
Dad!

22
00:01:19,860 --> 00:01:21,361
You're on your feet again.

23
00:01:21,486 --> 00:01:22,779
Thanks to your sister.

24
00:01:22,863 --> 00:01:24,406
I'm in no shape to fight,

25
00:01:24,573 --> 00:01:26,408
but maybe there is some way
I could help.

26
00:01:26,533 --> 00:01:27,701
Everything's going smoothly,

27
00:01:27,826 --> 00:01:29,703
and the eclipse hasn't even
kicked in yet.

28
00:01:29,828 --> 00:01:32,247
Let's hope
our luck holds out.

29
00:01:32,372 --> 00:01:34,291
Katara, you seem distracted.

30
00:01:34,583 --> 00:01:36,126
Is something wrong?

31
00:01:36,251 --> 00:01:37,252
Yeah.

32
00:01:37,377 --> 00:01:39,963
Is that―is that Aang?

33
00:01:40,088 --> 00:01:41,298
What?

34
00:01:41,423 --> 00:01:43,758
♪

35
00:01:43,884 --> 00:01:45,385
Please tell you're here
because the Fire Lord

36
00:01:45,510 --> 00:01:46,511
turned out to be a big wimp,

37
00:01:46,595 --> 00:01:48,722
and you didn't even need
the eclipse to take him down?

38
00:01:49,014 --> 00:01:50,307
He wasn't home.

39
00:01:50,557 --> 00:01:52,058
No one was.

40
00:01:52,142 --> 00:01:55,478
The entire palace city
is abandoned.

41
00:01:55,562 --> 00:01:56,730
They knew.

42
00:01:56,813 --> 00:01:58,023
AANG: It's over.

43
00:01:58,106 --> 00:02:00,191
The Fire Lord
is probably long gone.

44
00:02:00,317 --> 00:02:01,985
Far away on some remote island

45
00:02:02,110 --> 00:02:03,904
where he'll be safe
during the eclipse.

46
00:02:04,279 --> 00:02:05,572
No.

47
00:02:05,697 --> 00:02:07,574
My instincts tell me
he wouldn't go too far.

48
00:02:07,782 --> 00:02:09,159
He would have a secret bunker.

49
00:02:09,284 --> 00:02:11,369
Somewhere he could go, and it'll
be safe during a siege,

50
00:02:11,494 --> 00:02:13,496
but still be close enough
to lead his nation.

51
00:02:13,622 --> 00:02:15,248
If it's
an underground secret bunker

52
00:02:15,373 --> 00:02:18,376
we're looking for,
I'm just the girl to find it.

53
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:20,253
The Mechanist gave me
this timing device.

54
00:02:20,378 --> 00:02:21,671
It looks like we've got about
ten minutes

55
00:02:21,796 --> 00:02:22,964
until the full eclipse.

56
00:02:23,089 --> 00:02:24,841
Ten minutes to find
the Fire Lord.

57
00:02:24,966 --> 00:02:26,343
We can still do this.

58
00:02:26,468 --> 00:02:28,053
We can still win the day.

59
00:02:28,136 --> 00:02:29,137
Wait.

60
00:02:29,220 --> 00:02:31,681
If they knew we were coming,
it could all be a trap.

61
00:02:31,765 --> 00:02:33,808
Maybe we should use the time
we have left to make sure

62
00:02:33,892 --> 00:02:35,936
we all get out of here safely.

63
00:02:36,061 --> 00:02:37,812
Everyone who's here today
came prepared

64
00:02:37,938 --> 00:02:40,231
to risk everything
for this mission.

65
00:02:40,357 --> 00:02:42,108
They know what's at stake.

66
00:02:42,233 --> 00:02:45,111
If there's still a chance
and there's still hope,

67
00:02:45,236 --> 00:02:47,280
I think they would
want Aang to go for it.

68
00:02:47,405 --> 00:02:48,573
What do you think?

69
00:02:48,698 --> 00:02:50,075
You're the one
who has to face the Fire Lord.

70
00:02:50,492 --> 00:02:52,160
Whatever you decide,
I'm with you.

71
00:02:52,285 --> 00:02:55,538
♪

72
00:02:55,664 --> 00:02:58,458
I've got to try.

73
00:02:58,541 --> 00:03:00,794
[ roars ]

74
00:03:00,919 --> 00:03:03,838
♪

75
00:03:03,922 --> 00:03:05,548
Do you feel
anything down there?

76
00:03:05,882 --> 00:03:06,925
Yep.

77
00:03:07,050 --> 00:03:08,134
There are natural tunnels
crisscrossing

78
00:03:08,259 --> 00:03:09,928
through the inside
of the volcano.

79
00:03:10,053 --> 00:03:11,054
Anything else?

80
00:03:11,179 --> 00:03:12,555
Is there a structure somewhere?

81
00:03:15,183 --> 00:03:17,686
There's something big, dense,
and made of metal

82
00:03:17,811 --> 00:03:19,562
deep in the heart
of the volcano.

83
00:03:19,688 --> 00:03:21,398
Sounds like
a secret bunker to me.

84
00:03:22,607 --> 00:03:23,942
[ crash ]

85
00:03:25,485 --> 00:03:26,695
Stay safe.

86
00:03:26,820 --> 00:03:28,279
We'll be back soon.

87
00:03:30,782 --> 00:03:32,117
This way!
That one's a dead end.

88
00:03:32,242 --> 00:03:33,910
SOKKA: What would we do without you?

89
00:03:34,035 --> 00:03:35,829
Perish and burn in hot magma.

90
00:03:35,954 --> 00:03:37,205
Yeah, pretty much.

91
00:03:40,917 --> 00:03:42,627
TOPH: The tunnel continues
on the other side

92
00:03:42,752 --> 00:03:44,337
and it leads
right to the bunker.

93
00:03:44,462 --> 00:03:46,256
We'll have to be
fast but careful.

94
00:03:46,381 --> 00:03:47,841
Ah!

95
00:03:47,966 --> 00:03:49,300
How was that careful?

96
00:03:49,426 --> 00:03:50,510
I was wrong.

97
00:03:50,635 --> 00:03:52,762
We need to be fast,
careful, and lucky.

98
00:03:52,887 --> 00:03:55,015
♪

99
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:59,602
[ lava hissing ]

100
00:03:59,728 --> 00:04:00,895
SOKKA: There's no floor!

101
00:04:01,021 --> 00:04:03,481
It's just a river of lava.

102
00:04:03,565 --> 00:04:05,942
AANG: Climb aboard
and hold on tight.

103
00:04:06,026 --> 00:04:08,069
[ screaming ]

104
00:04:08,153 --> 00:04:12,657
♪

105
00:04:20,081 --> 00:04:21,708
SOKKA: That's some door!

106
00:04:21,833 --> 00:04:25,211
♪

107
00:04:25,295 --> 00:04:26,504
[ metal banging ]

108
00:04:26,629 --> 00:04:27,964
Not a problem.

109
00:04:28,089 --> 00:04:29,257
♪

110
00:04:29,382 --> 00:04:31,009
[ metal banging ]

111
00:04:31,134 --> 00:04:33,678
♪

112
00:04:33,803 --> 00:04:36,306
[ metal banging ]

113
00:04:37,891 --> 00:04:40,852
I am so glad we
added you to the group.

114
00:04:40,935 --> 00:04:44,939
♪

115
00:04:47,567 --> 00:04:51,821
[ missiles exploding ]

116
00:04:54,324 --> 00:04:59,204
[ crash ]

117
00:04:59,370 --> 00:05:03,875
♪

118
00:05:03,958 --> 00:05:05,043
Retreat!

119
00:05:05,126 --> 00:05:07,128
Everyone move to the secondary
defensive position!

120
00:05:07,212 --> 00:05:08,379
Retreat!

121
00:05:08,588 --> 00:05:11,049
♪

122
00:05:11,758 --> 00:05:13,927
The eclipse
is only minutes away.

123
00:05:14,010 --> 00:05:17,097
We should be able to make it up
the hill by the time it starts

124
00:05:17,180 --> 00:05:20,391
and secure the entire palace
by the time it's finished!

125
00:05:20,475 --> 00:05:23,978
MEN: [ screaming ]

126
00:05:24,229 --> 00:05:25,897
We can wait here if you want.

127
00:05:25,980 --> 00:05:28,691
No. I want to press forward
with the others.

128
00:05:32,779 --> 00:05:35,615
[ whistling ]

129
00:05:35,740 --> 00:05:37,367
[ gasps ]

130
00:05:37,492 --> 00:05:40,036
♪

131
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:42,122
The Fire Lord's chamber
is that way down the hall

132
00:05:42,205 --> 00:05:45,083
to the left and up the stairs.
You can't miss it.

133
00:05:45,208 --> 00:05:46,626
Thanks.

134
00:05:50,505 --> 00:05:52,841
[ sighs ]

135
00:05:52,966 --> 00:05:54,384
[ whistles ]

136
00:05:54,509 --> 00:05:57,137
♪

137
00:05:57,220 --> 00:05:59,305
Only 30 seconds
until the total eclipse.

138
00:05:59,430 --> 00:06:03,268
♪

139
00:06:03,393 --> 00:06:05,270
[ deep breathing ]

140
00:06:05,770 --> 00:06:07,063
I'm ready.

141
00:06:07,147 --> 00:06:09,983
I'm ready to face the Fire Lord.

142
00:06:10,066 --> 00:06:13,153
[ door opens ]

143
00:06:13,236 --> 00:06:15,572
So, you are alive after all.

144
00:06:15,655 --> 00:06:17,824
♪

145
00:06:17,907 --> 00:06:19,826
I had a hunch
that you survived.

146
00:06:19,909 --> 00:06:20,994
But it doesn't matter,

147
00:06:21,119 --> 00:06:23,121
I've known about the invasion
for months.

148
00:06:23,288 --> 00:06:27,333
♪

149
00:06:28,877 --> 00:06:30,336
I'm ready to face you.

150
00:06:30,587 --> 00:06:35,008
♪

151
00:06:35,175 --> 00:06:38,052
Prince Zuko,
what are you doing here?

152
00:06:38,469 --> 00:06:40,597
♪

153
00:06:43,558 --> 00:06:47,854
♪

154
00:06:53,234 --> 00:06:55,320
The eclipse is starting!

155
00:06:55,445 --> 00:06:57,113
Put on your eclipse glasses.

156
00:06:57,238 --> 00:07:02,285
♪

157
00:07:10,126 --> 00:07:12,337
Why are you here?

158
00:07:12,462 --> 00:07:14,130
I'm here to tell the truth.

159
00:07:14,255 --> 00:07:17,800
Telling the truth
during the middle of an eclipse.

160
00:07:17,926 --> 00:07:19,844
This should be interesting.

161
00:07:25,391 --> 00:07:27,268
First of all, in Ba Sing Se,

162
00:07:27,393 --> 00:07:30,647
it was Azula who took down
the Avatar, not me.

163
00:07:30,772 --> 00:07:32,899
Why would she
lie to me about that?

164
00:07:33,024 --> 00:07:34,776
Because the Avatar
is not dead.

165
00:07:34,901 --> 00:07:36,152
He survived.

166
00:07:36,277 --> 00:07:37,528
What?

167
00:07:37,654 --> 00:07:39,739
In fact, he's probably
is leading this invasion.

168
00:07:39,864 --> 00:07:41,449
He could be on us right now.

169
00:07:41,574 --> 00:07:42,867
Get out!

170
00:07:42,951 --> 00:07:45,578
Get out of my sight right now
if you know what's good for you.

171
00:07:45,703 --> 00:07:46,746
That's another thing.

172
00:07:46,871 --> 00:07:49,040
I'm not taking orders
from you anymore.

173
00:07:49,165 --> 00:07:51,167
You will obey me

174
00:07:51,292 --> 00:07:54,337
or this defiant breath
will be your last!

175
00:07:56,339 --> 00:07:57,840
Think again!

176
00:07:57,966 --> 00:08:00,843
I am going to speak my mind,
and you are going to listen!

177
00:08:00,969 --> 00:08:03,388
♪

178
00:08:03,513 --> 00:08:04,597
Where is he?

179
00:08:04,722 --> 00:08:06,766
Where is the Fire Lord?

180
00:08:06,891 --> 00:08:08,977
Hm, you mean I'm not
good enough for you?

181
00:08:09,102 --> 00:08:11,312
You're hurting my feelings.

182
00:08:11,437 --> 00:08:14,190
Stop wasting our time
and give us the information.

183
00:08:14,315 --> 00:08:17,110
You're powerless right now, so
you're in no position to refuse.

184
00:08:17,235 --> 00:08:18,778
And stick to the truth.

185
00:08:18,903 --> 00:08:21,072
I'll be able to tell
if you're lying.

186
00:08:21,197 --> 00:08:22,282
Are you sure?

187
00:08:22,407 --> 00:08:24,701
I'm a pretty good liar.

188
00:08:24,826 --> 00:08:27,578
I am a 400-foot-tall
purple platypus bear

189
00:08:27,704 --> 00:08:31,249
with pink horns
and silver wings.

190
00:08:31,374 --> 00:08:32,792
Okay, you're good, I admit it.

191
00:08:35,920 --> 00:08:38,548
But you really ought to consider
telling the truth anyway.

192
00:08:38,673 --> 00:08:41,259
♪

193
00:08:41,384 --> 00:08:44,095
[ crash ]

194
00:08:46,389 --> 00:08:49,517
When I left Ba Sing Se,
I brought home some souvenirs.

195
00:08:49,684 --> 00:08:51,561
♪

196
00:08:51,686 --> 00:08:53,229
Dai Li agents.

197
00:08:53,354 --> 00:08:57,734
♪

198
00:09:07,243 --> 00:09:09,037
Surround the periphery!

199
00:09:09,287 --> 00:09:12,540
We have to secure the palace
by the time the eclipse is over.

200
00:09:12,665 --> 00:09:15,752
Otherwise, we'll be in
for the fight of our lives.

201
00:09:20,548 --> 00:09:21,799
TYRO: Stop!

202
00:09:21,924 --> 00:09:24,135
Surrender peacefully,
and we won't harm you.

203
00:09:24,469 --> 00:09:25,928
We'll never surrender.

204
00:09:26,054 --> 00:09:30,058
♪

205
00:09:31,225 --> 00:09:32,769
Er, okay, we surrender.

206
00:09:32,894 --> 00:09:34,979
♪

207
00:09:35,104 --> 00:09:36,147
HAKODA: There it is.

208
00:09:36,272 --> 00:09:38,232
The Fire Nation royal palace.

209
00:09:38,358 --> 00:09:39,984
We've come so far.

210
00:09:40,109 --> 00:09:41,569
It's not over yet.

211
00:09:41,694 --> 00:09:44,530
♪

212
00:09:44,655 --> 00:09:46,199
For so long, all I wanted

213
00:09:46,324 --> 00:09:48,826
was for you to love me,
to accept me.

214
00:09:48,951 --> 00:09:50,745
I thought it was my honor
that I wanted.

215
00:09:50,870 --> 00:09:54,165
But really, I was just
trying to please you.

216
00:09:54,290 --> 00:09:58,920
You, my father, who banished me
just for talking out of turn.

217
00:09:59,045 --> 00:10:02,131
My father, who challenged me―
a 13-year-old boy―

218
00:10:02,256 --> 00:10:03,674
to an Agni Kai.

219
00:10:03,800 --> 00:10:06,677
How can you possibly
justify a duel with a child?

220
00:10:06,803 --> 00:10:08,554
It was to teach you respect.

221
00:10:08,679 --> 00:10:09,722
It was cruel!

222
00:10:09,847 --> 00:10:10,932
And it was wrong!

223
00:10:11,057 --> 00:10:12,600
Then you've learned nothing.

224
00:10:12,725 --> 00:10:15,353
No, I've learnt everything!

225
00:10:15,478 --> 00:10:17,647
And I had to learn it on my own.

226
00:10:17,772 --> 00:10:19,774
Growing up, we were taught
that the Fire Nation

227
00:10:19,899 --> 00:10:22,276
was the greatest civilization
in history.

228
00:10:22,402 --> 00:10:25,071
And somehow, the war was our way
of sharing our greatness

229
00:10:25,196 --> 00:10:27,240
with the rest of the world.

230
00:10:27,365 --> 00:10:29,742
What an amazing lie that was.

231
00:10:29,867 --> 00:10:32,870
The people of the world are
terrified by the Fire Nation!

232
00:10:32,995 --> 00:10:35,623
They don't see our greatness,
they hate us!

233
00:10:35,748 --> 00:10:36,999
And we deserve it.

234
00:10:37,125 --> 00:10:39,669
We've created an era
of fear in the world.

235
00:10:39,794 --> 00:10:42,672
And if we don't want the world
to destroy itself,

236
00:10:42,797 --> 00:10:47,343
we need to replace it with
an era of peace and kindness.

237
00:10:47,468 --> 00:10:49,595
[ laughing ]

238
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:52,348
Your Uncle has gotten to you,
hasn't he?

239
00:10:53,975 --> 00:10:56,436
Yes. He has.

240
00:10:59,522 --> 00:11:01,858
[ crash ]

241
00:11:01,983 --> 00:11:05,278
♪

242
00:11:07,780 --> 00:11:10,158
[ rock crumbling ]

243
00:11:10,283 --> 00:11:14,620
♪

244
00:11:35,099 --> 00:11:36,392
[ crash ]

245
00:11:36,517 --> 00:11:38,478
[ grunts ]

246
00:11:38,603 --> 00:11:42,398
[ rocks crashing ]

247
00:11:42,523 --> 00:11:48,488
♪

248
00:12:00,333 --> 00:12:06,047
♪

249
00:12:20,144 --> 00:12:21,270
I can't pin her down.

250
00:12:21,395 --> 00:12:22,772
She's too quick.

251
00:12:22,897 --> 00:12:27,235
♪

252
00:12:31,948 --> 00:12:34,867
[ grunting ]

253
00:12:37,495 --> 00:12:40,498
Wait! Aang, Toph,
stop attacking.

254
00:12:40,623 --> 00:12:41,749
Don't you see what she's doing?

255
00:12:41,874 --> 00:12:43,292
She's just playing with us.

256
00:12:43,417 --> 00:12:45,336
She's not even trying
to win this fight!

257
00:12:45,461 --> 00:12:48,172
Not true, I'm
giving it my all.

258
00:12:48,297 --> 00:12:50,758
You're trying to keep us here
and waste all our time!

259
00:12:50,883 --> 00:12:52,009
Um, right.

260
00:12:52,134 --> 00:12:54,053
I think your friend
just said that, genius.

261
00:12:54,178 --> 00:12:55,388
And since you can't see,

262
00:12:55,513 --> 00:12:58,349
I should tell you
I'm rolling my eyes.

263
00:12:58,474 --> 00:13:00,101
I'll roll your whole head!

264
00:13:00,226 --> 00:13:01,852
She's just baiting you again.

265
00:13:01,978 --> 00:13:03,521
Okay, so what do we do?

266
00:13:03,646 --> 00:13:05,022
Just ignore her?

267
00:13:05,147 --> 00:13:07,608
We don't have a choice,
we just have to get out of here

268
00:13:07,733 --> 00:13:10,528
and find the Fire Lord
on our own somehow.

269
00:13:10,611 --> 00:13:11,654
It's a trap.

270
00:13:11,779 --> 00:13:13,406
Don't say I didn't warn you.

271
00:13:13,531 --> 00:13:15,408
Ignore!

272
00:13:15,533 --> 00:13:17,994
So, Sokka's your name, right?

273
00:13:18,119 --> 00:13:21,706
My favorite prisoner used
to mention you all the time.

274
00:13:21,831 --> 00:13:24,208
She was convinced that you were
going to come rescue her.

275
00:13:24,333 --> 00:13:28,337
Of course, you never came,
and she gave up on you.

276
00:13:28,462 --> 00:13:31,549
[ grunting ]

277
00:13:31,674 --> 00:13:33,092
Come and get it.

278
00:13:33,217 --> 00:13:36,679
♪

279
00:13:36,804 --> 00:13:39,390
[ grunts ]

280
00:13:39,515 --> 00:13:42,518
Where is Suki?

281
00:13:44,145 --> 00:13:46,480
ZUKO: After I leave here today,
I'm going to free Uncle Iroh

282
00:13:46,606 --> 00:13:47,690
from his prison.

283
00:13:47,815 --> 00:13:49,817
And I'm going to beg
for his forgiveness.

284
00:13:49,942 --> 00:13:52,069
He is the one who has been
a real father to me.

285
00:13:52,194 --> 00:13:54,697
[ chuckles ]
That's just beautiful.

286
00:13:54,822 --> 00:13:58,284
Maybe he can pass down to you
the ways of tea and failure.

287
00:13:58,409 --> 00:14:00,494
But I've come to an even more
important decision.

288
00:14:02,121 --> 00:14:03,956
I'm going to join the Avatar.

289
00:14:04,081 --> 00:14:05,791
And I'm going to help him
defeat you.

290
00:14:05,916 --> 00:14:07,293
Really?

291
00:14:07,418 --> 00:14:09,629
Since you're
a full-blown traitor now,

292
00:14:09,754 --> 00:14:11,881
and you want me gone, why wait?

293
00:14:12,006 --> 00:14:15,009
I'm powerless,
you've got your swords,

294
00:14:15,134 --> 00:14:17,094
why don't you just do it now?

295
00:14:17,219 --> 00:14:19,180
Because I know
my own destiny.

296
00:14:19,305 --> 00:14:22,016
Taking you down
is the Avatar's destiny.

297
00:14:22,141 --> 00:14:23,726
[ metal clangs ]

298
00:14:23,851 --> 00:14:25,561
Goodbye.

299
00:14:25,686 --> 00:14:27,730
Coward! You think
you're brave enough to face me,

300
00:14:27,855 --> 00:14:29,982
but you'll only do it
during the eclipse.

301
00:14:30,107 --> 00:14:31,776
If you have any real courage,

302
00:14:31,901 --> 00:14:34,695
you'll stick around
until the Sun comes out.

303
00:14:34,820 --> 00:14:38,032
Don't you want to know
what happened to your mother?

304
00:14:38,157 --> 00:14:40,910
♪

305
00:14:51,295 --> 00:14:53,005
ZUKO: What happened that night?

306
00:14:53,130 --> 00:14:56,592
My father―Fire Lord Azulon―
had commanded me

307
00:14:56,717 --> 00:15:01,013
to do the unthinkable to you,
my own son.

308
00:15:01,138 --> 00:15:03,057
And I was going to do it.

309
00:15:03,182 --> 00:15:04,475
Your Mother found out

310
00:15:04,600 --> 00:15:07,645
and swore she would
protect you at any cost.

311
00:15:07,770 --> 00:15:11,190
She knew I wanted the throne,
and she proposed a plan.

312
00:15:11,315 --> 00:15:14,610
A plan in which I would become
Fire Lord

313
00:15:14,735 --> 00:15:18,114
and your life would be spared.

314
00:15:18,239 --> 00:15:20,366
Where's Suki?

315
00:15:20,491 --> 00:15:21,867
Answer me!

316
00:15:21,992 --> 00:15:25,287
Sokka, she won't talk.

317
00:15:25,413 --> 00:15:27,081
Where are you keeping her?

318
00:15:28,165 --> 00:15:31,627
Your Mother did vicious,
treasonous things that night.

319
00:15:32,128 --> 00:15:34,797
She knew the consequences
and accepted them.

320
00:15:34,922 --> 00:15:38,509
For her treason,
she was banished.

321
00:15:38,634 --> 00:15:40,010
So she's alive.

322
00:15:40,136 --> 00:15:42,221
Perhaps.

323
00:15:42,346 --> 00:15:46,225
Now I realize that banishment
is far too merciful a penalty

324
00:15:46,350 --> 00:15:47,935
for treason.

325
00:15:48,060 --> 00:15:51,397
Your penalty
will be far steeper.

326
00:15:51,522 --> 00:15:54,316
♪

327
00:15:54,442 --> 00:16:00,239
[ lightning zapping ]

328
00:16:01,490 --> 00:16:04,034
-[ explosion ]
-[ grunts ]

329
00:16:04,326 --> 00:16:09,415
♪

330
00:16:12,585 --> 00:16:14,879
Oh. Sounds like
the fire-bending's back on.

331
00:16:15,004 --> 00:16:18,090
[ grunting ]

332
00:16:18,215 --> 00:16:21,802
♪

333
00:16:24,555 --> 00:16:26,182
Dad's all the way
at the end of the hall

334
00:16:26,265 --> 00:16:28,100
and down the secret stairway
on the left.

335
00:16:28,225 --> 00:16:31,270
I'm sure he'll be more
than happy to see you now.

336
00:16:31,395 --> 00:16:32,605
SOKKA: I fell for it!

337
00:16:32,730 --> 00:16:34,482
I used up all our time.

338
00:16:34,607 --> 00:16:36,358
It's not your fault, Sokka.

339
00:16:36,484 --> 00:16:37,985
Azula was ready for us.

340
00:16:38,110 --> 00:16:40,613
She had every move planned out.

341
00:16:40,738 --> 00:16:42,323
And now it's too late.

342
00:16:42,448 --> 00:16:44,450
AANG: Maybe it's not too late.

343
00:16:44,575 --> 00:16:47,828
The eclipse is over, but I can
face the Fire Lord anyway.

344
00:16:47,953 --> 00:16:48,954
No.

345
00:16:49,038 --> 00:16:50,164
I don't think
that's a good idea.

346
00:16:50,289 --> 00:16:51,624
But I'm ready!

347
00:16:51,707 --> 00:16:55,085
I came here with a job to do,
and everyone's counting on me.

348
00:16:55,211 --> 00:16:57,296
The Fire Lord knew
we were coming this time.

349
00:16:57,421 --> 00:16:59,882
We thought we had surprise
on our side, but we didn't.

350
00:17:00,007 --> 00:17:01,425
It just wasn't our day.

351
00:17:01,550 --> 00:17:04,512
What we need to do now
is go help our friends.

352
00:17:04,637 --> 00:17:06,055
I guess you guys are right.

353
00:17:06,180 --> 00:17:07,515
SOKKA: You'll have another chance.

354
00:17:07,640 --> 00:17:09,099
I know you will.

355
00:17:14,146 --> 00:17:15,397
BATO: What should we do, Hakoda?

356
00:17:15,523 --> 00:17:17,191
Shouldn't something
have happened by now?

357
00:17:17,316 --> 00:17:18,442
I don't know.

358
00:17:18,567 --> 00:17:20,152
But now that the eclipse
is over,

359
00:17:20,277 --> 00:17:23,656
I expect we're going to see
some Firebenders any minute.

360
00:17:23,906 --> 00:17:28,035
♪

361
00:17:32,289 --> 00:17:34,208
MECHANIST: My own invention.

362
00:17:34,542 --> 00:17:36,085
Oh, this is terrible!

363
00:17:36,210 --> 00:17:42,132
♪

364
00:17:48,097 --> 00:17:49,348
They're back!

365
00:17:49,473 --> 00:17:55,396
♪

366
00:18:03,320 --> 00:18:04,780
It was all a trap.

367
00:18:04,905 --> 00:18:07,658
Azula knew we were coming, and
she's plotted out every move.

368
00:18:08,534 --> 00:18:10,786
We just got to get to the beach
as fast as we can.

369
00:18:10,995 --> 00:18:12,079
If we can make it
to the submarines,

370
00:18:12,162 --> 00:18:13,539
maybe we can get away safely.

371
00:18:13,664 --> 00:18:16,125
They've got air power,
but so do I!

372
00:18:16,250 --> 00:18:18,168
♪

373
00:18:18,294 --> 00:18:20,254
I'm going to do what I can
to slow them down.

374
00:18:23,299 --> 00:18:25,175
Appa, you and I can help, too.

375
00:18:25,301 --> 00:18:28,178
♪

376
00:18:28,304 --> 00:18:30,472
Everyone, let's get back
to the subs!

377
00:18:30,598 --> 00:18:35,394
♪

378
00:18:48,908 --> 00:18:51,535
[ gunfire exploding ]

379
00:18:51,660 --> 00:18:56,248
[ growling ]

380
00:18:56,373 --> 00:19:00,002
♪

381
00:19:00,127 --> 00:19:01,462
KATARA: We can't keep them all back.

382
00:19:01,587 --> 00:19:03,464
They're too many of them!

383
00:19:03,589 --> 00:19:04,924
Let's join the others.

384
00:19:05,049 --> 00:19:09,929
♪

385
00:19:17,436 --> 00:19:18,437
Uncle!

386
00:19:18,562 --> 00:19:23,525
♪

387
00:19:23,651 --> 00:19:24,902
Where is my Uncle?

388
00:19:25,027 --> 00:19:26,320
He's gone.

389
00:19:26,445 --> 00:19:28,280
He busted himself out.

390
00:19:28,405 --> 00:19:30,115
I―I've never seen
anything like it!

391
00:19:30,240 --> 00:19:32,701
He was like a one man army!

392
00:19:32,826 --> 00:19:38,207
♪

393
00:19:40,125 --> 00:19:41,293
Try and find cover!

394
00:19:41,418 --> 00:19:42,962
I think we're about
to see some bombs.

395
00:19:43,087 --> 00:19:47,758
♪

396
00:19:49,426 --> 00:19:54,723
[ bombs exploding ]

397
00:19:54,848 --> 00:19:56,684
♪

398
00:19:56,809 --> 00:20:00,854
MEN: [ screaming ]

399
00:20:02,773 --> 00:20:05,567
KATARA: Why aren't they turning around
to attack us again?

400
00:20:06,151 --> 00:20:08,445
They're headed for the beach.

401
00:20:08,570 --> 00:20:10,239
They're going to destroy
the submarines!

402
00:20:10,364 --> 00:20:11,865
How are we all
going to escape?

403
00:20:11,991 --> 00:20:13,701
We're not.

404
00:20:14,159 --> 00:20:16,453
Then our only choice
is to stand and fight.

405
00:20:16,578 --> 00:20:19,331
We have the Avatar,
we could still win!

406
00:20:19,456 --> 00:20:23,335
Yes, with the Avatar we could
still win on another day.

407
00:20:23,460 --> 00:20:24,920
You kids have to leave.

408
00:20:25,045 --> 00:20:27,047
You have to escape
on Appa together.

409
00:20:27,172 --> 00:20:28,173
What?

410
00:20:28,298 --> 00:20:29,883
We can't leave you behind.

411
00:20:30,009 --> 00:20:32,136
We won't leave anyone behind.

412
00:20:32,261 --> 00:20:34,388
You're our only chance
in the long run.

413
00:20:34,513 --> 00:20:37,099
You and Sokka have to go
with Aang somewhere safe.

414
00:20:37,224 --> 00:20:39,518
It's the only way
to keep hope alive.

415
00:20:39,643 --> 00:20:42,021
The youngest of our group
should go with you.

416
00:20:42,146 --> 00:20:44,773
The adults will stay behind
and surrender.

417
00:20:44,898 --> 00:20:48,861
We'll be prisoners, but we'll
all survive this battle.

418
00:20:48,986 --> 00:20:52,114
I've got some experience
with the Fire Nation prisons.

419
00:20:52,239 --> 00:20:54,908
It's not going to be easy,
but we'll get by.

420
00:20:55,034 --> 00:20:56,201
They're at the beach already!

421
00:20:56,535 --> 00:21:01,123
♪

422
00:21:06,712 --> 00:21:10,674
[ bombs exploding ]

423
00:21:20,184 --> 00:21:24,021
[ explosions continue ]

424
00:21:24,271 --> 00:21:29,735
♪

425
00:21:36,867 --> 00:21:38,077
Bye, son.

426
00:21:38,202 --> 00:21:39,495
Bye, Dad.

427
00:21:39,620 --> 00:21:41,371
I'm really proud of you.

428
00:21:41,497 --> 00:21:44,666
♪

429
00:21:44,792 --> 00:21:47,127
[ grunts ]
I'll miss you, Pipsqueak.

430
00:21:47,252 --> 00:21:48,796
Take care, The Duke.

431
00:21:50,923 --> 00:21:52,341
We'll be back for you, Dad.

432
00:21:52,466 --> 00:21:54,510
If we don't escape
on our own first.

433
00:21:54,635 --> 00:21:57,805
♪

434
00:21:57,930 --> 00:22:01,266
We lost today,
but we've never been this close.

435
00:22:01,391 --> 00:22:04,728
We tasted victory,
and that counts for something.

436
00:22:04,853 --> 00:22:06,730
We'll miss you, Dad.

437
00:22:08,065 --> 00:22:09,108
SOKKA: Bye, Dad.

438
00:22:09,358 --> 00:22:11,151
We won't be apart
for too long this time.

439
00:22:11,276 --> 00:22:12,861
I promise.

440
00:22:12,986 --> 00:22:18,909
♪

441
00:22:23,372 --> 00:22:27,084
Thank you all for being
so brave and so strong.

442
00:22:27,209 --> 00:22:28,710
I'm going to make this
up to you.

443
00:22:31,296 --> 00:22:36,301
[ growling ]

444
00:22:36,426 --> 00:22:41,098
♪

445
00:22:45,811 --> 00:22:47,229
Should we follow them,
Princess?

446
00:22:47,354 --> 00:22:49,314
AZULA: No. They're too fast.

447
00:22:49,439 --> 00:22:51,608
It doesn't matter,
they'll be back.

448
00:22:51,733 --> 00:22:54,945
♪

449
00:22:55,070 --> 00:22:56,613
I know just the place
for us to go

450
00:22:56,697 --> 00:22:58,073
where we'll be safe for a while.

451
00:22:58,198 --> 00:22:59,658
The Western Air Temple.

452
00:22:59,783 --> 00:23:01,076
[ grunting ]

453
00:23:04,121 --> 00:23:09,585
♪

454
00:23:20,053 --> 00:23:24,558
MALE:
[ vocalizing drumbeats ]

455
00:23:30,480 --> 00:23:37,196
♪

456
00:23:53,545 --> 00:24:00,052
♪
